.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt PATINA-DESKTOP 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-desktop
.Nd the Patina desktop: its pieces, and how to look after them
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The Patina desktop is a floating Wayland desktop in the style of the Patina
apps.
It is made of small programs, each a separate process, so that one going
wrong can be restarted without the others:
.Bl -tag -width "patina-night-light(1)"
.It Xr patina-session 1
The login session.
Runs the compositor, and starts it again when it restarts or crashes.
.It Xr patina-compositor 1
The compositor: the screen, keyboard and pointer, windows, and the
desktop's own keys.
It starts the wallpaper, the bar and the tiler, and keeps track of every
piece it starts.
.It Xr patina-tiler 1
How windows tile: dragged to an edge, or with Super and an arrow.
.It Xr patina-raise 1
Focuses an app's window, or starts the app: Alt+B for Firefox.
.It Xr patina-bar 1
The bar: the launcher button, the pinned apps and a tab per window, which
drag into another order, the tray and the clock.
Its config file holds the settings the whole shell shares.
.It Xr patina-wallpaper 1
The wallpaper behind every window.
.It Xr patina-menu 1
The desktop's menu, on a right click on the empty desktop.
.It Xr patina-volume 1
The volume menu, which also flashes up after a volume or brightness key.
.It Xr patina-wifi 1
The Wi-Fi menu.
.It Xr patina-clock 1
The clock's menu: a month, and the day's events from the Calendar app.
.It Xr patina-power 1
The power menu, after the bar's clock: Lock, Log Out, Restart and Shut
Down.
.It Xr patina-lock 1
The lock screen.
.It Xr patina-dictate 1
Dictation: hold Ctrl+Super+Alt and speak, and what was said is typed into the
focused window, transcribed on the machine with Whisper.
.It Xr patina-settings 1
Settings: the skin, wallpaper, default apps, Night Light, power modes, and
the desktop's processes.
.It Xr patina-processes 1
The process manager, on Ctrl+Shift+Escape: what's running, what it costs, and
ending it; graphs of the CPU, memory, disks and network.
.It Xr patina-night-light 1
Night Light from the command line.
.El
.Pp
The launcher, opened by the bar's flask button or by tapping Super, is
.Xr patina-launcher 1 ,
built from its own repository.
.Sh STARTING THE DESKTOP
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \&At the login screen
.Ql make install
installs the desktop for every user of the machine and adds a
.Dq Patina
session to the login screen, which runs
.Ql patina-session --session .
Choose it from the session button on the password screen.
.It From a text console
Log in and run
.Nm patina-session ,
or
.Nm patina-compositor
to have no restarts.
.It Nested in another desktop
Run
.Nm patina-compositor
from a terminal on GNOME, sway or dwl: it opens as a window there.
This is how the pieces are tried during development.
.El
.Sh WHERE THINGS ARE KEPT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-dictate/config.toml
Where dictation's overlay shows, which Settings' Dictation page writes.
See
.Xr patina-dictate 1 .
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-compositor/config.toml
The compositor's settings: scale, keyboard, touchpad, cursor, media keys,
lock screen, when the screen turns off, Night Light and key bindings.
Written with every setting commented out on first start.
Saving it applies it within a second.
See
.Xr patina-compositor 1 .
.It Pa ~/.local/state/patina-tiler/windows.toml
Where each app's window was last, so it reopens there.
See
.Xr patina-tiler 1 .
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml
The bar's settings, and the shell's: the skin and the wallpaper, which the
desktop's menu and Settings write.
See
.Xr patina-bar 1 .
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/skins/
Skins of your own, beside Patina's built-in ones.
.It Pa ~/Pictures/Screenshots/
Screenshots, from Super+Shift+3, Super+Shift+4 and Print.
.It Pa ~/Pictures/Wallpapers/
Images offered as wallpapers, with the system's backgrounds.
.It Pa ~/.config/patina/defaults.toml
The default apps chosen on Settings' Defaults page, a line per kind, such as
.Ql browser = \(dqfirefox\(dq .
They're written out as
.Pa ~/.config/patina-mimeapps.list ,
which only this desktop reads, so other desktops keep their own, and which
comes before an app's Open With choices.
Settings writes it at once; a change by hand applies from the next session.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/applications/patina-mimeapps.list
Which app opens a file when no choice of your own says otherwise:
images in an image viewer, folders in Files.
Installed by
.Ql make install
and read only in this desktop.
Choices made with an app's Open With, kept in
.Pa ~/.config/mimeapps.list ,
come first; to change one by hand, run
.Ql xdg-mime default org.gnome.Loupe.desktop image/png .
.El
.Sh RESTARTING AND RECOVERING
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It An app hangs
Press
.Sy Ctrl+Shift+Escape
for the process manager,
.Xr patina-processes 1 ,
even over a fullscreen game; choose the app and press Delete to end it, or
Shift+Delete to kill it.
.It A piece misbehaves
Open Settings at its Processes page
.Pq Ql patina-settings --page processes .
It lists what the compositor started, with each one's state and output;
Restart and Stop act on one.
The wallpaper, the bar and the tiler come back on their own when they exit,
so
.Ql pkill patina-bar
also restarts the bar, from the binary now installed.
.It The compositor is to be restarted
Press
.Sy Ctrl+Alt+Shift+Backspace ,
or use Restart Desktop at the bottom of the Processes page.
Every window closes and its app quits; the desktop comes back without
logging out.
This needs
.Xr patina-session 1 ,
.Xr patina-tiler 1 ,
as at the login screen.
After
.Ql make install ,
that is all a change to the compositor takes.
.It The compositor crashes
.Xr patina-session 1
starts it again a second later; three crashes within a minute end the
session, back at the login screen.
A screen that was locked is locked again.
.It The screen is frozen or black
Switch to a text console with Ctrl+Alt+F3, log in, and run
.Ql pkill patina-session
to end the session and return to the login screen.
.Ql pkill patina-compositor
only restarts the desktop.
.It Leaving
Log Out in the power menu, after the bar's clock.
.Sy Ctrl+Alt+Backspace
also quits the compositor and ends the session, whatever state it's in.
.El
.Pp
The pieces' output is in the session's log:
.Ql journalctl -b | grep patina
under GDM, with each line prefixed by the piece that wrote it.
The Processes page shows the last 500 lines of each.
